  "title": "Can Police Take Your Property Without a Conviction? #Shorts",
  "description": "Civil forfeiture can let the government take your car, your cash, even your house — without ever convicting you of a crime.\n\nAn Indiana man's $42,000 SUV, bought with his late father's life-insurance money, was seized over a small drug sale — about four times the most he could be fined.\n\nIn Timbs v. Indiana (2019), the Supreme Court ruled 9-0 that the ban on excessive fines applies to the states too. He got his car back.\n\nWatch the full story on the channel.\n\n#Shorts #SupremeCourt #CivilForfeiture #Timbs #EighthAmendment #Law #Documentary",
